<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Nabigha al-Dhubyani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Nabigha al-Dhubyani was a pre-Islamic Arab poet of the 6th century, counted in some collections among the poets of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muallaqat">Mu'allaqat</a>. He lived for long periods at the courts of the Lakhmid king al-Nu'man III at al-Hira and of the Ghassanid rulers, writing praise poems and apologies after he fell from favour. At the fair of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souq-ukaz">Ukaz</a> he was said to judge between rival poets.</p></div>
